From: Trijal Saha <97483939+Trijal08@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] samsung-sit: cap registration queries in flight at stock's two

Stock never has more than two registration queries outstanding -- one
GET_VOICE_REGISTRATION and one GET_DATA_REGISTRATION -- in any of five
captures, while sending *more* of them than we do:

                 0x0700  0x0701   max in flight
    stock            33      36        2
    stock            50      52        2
    stock            32      34        2
    ours             23      30        9
    ours             27      31        7

So the divergence was never volume, it was that we had no cap: several
callers poll independently and nothing serialises them now that requests
are pipelined. We peaked at nine.

These are reads of the current state, so the first caller of each kind now
issues the query and the rest share its answer. One round trip is the right
answer for everyone who asked inside it, the duplicate work goes away, and
the cap falls out at exactly stock's two.

Why it matters here: stock's SETUP_DATA_CALL for `ims` has no registration
query beside it and is answered in 1.0-2.6s; ours has had one to six and
takes 2.9-10.9s. So this also drains the last of them immediately before
that frame is built -- which is where the check has to be. r64 gated where
the IMS sequence *decides* to ask, but between that and the frame are a cid
acquire, the data preference, the attach re-assert and the profile push, and
other callers issue queries inside those tens of milliseconds. r64's gate
therefore never engaged once on hardware and changed nothing: in flight 3
and 7, latency 2829ms and 7889ms, against r63's 3 and 7 at 2898ms and
7908ms. That patch is dropped rather than kept.

Still not claimed as the cause of the latency: the count does not order it
within our own data. What is claimed is that the cap is what stock does.

--- a/src/plugins/samsung-sit/mm-port-serial-sit.c
+++ b/src/plugins/samsung-sit/mm-port-serial-sit.c
@@ -353,6 +353,38 @@
     tx_push (self, request);
 }
 
+/*
+ * How many of `ids` are written and still unanswered.
+ *
+ * Stock never has a registration query in flight when it asks for an IMS
+ * context; see mm_sit_client_registration_queries_in_flight().
+ */
+guint
+mm_port_serial_sit_pending_count (MMPortSerialSit *self,
+                                  const guint16   *ids,
+                                  gsize            n_ids)
+{
+    GHashTableIter iter;
+    gpointer       value;
+    guint          n = 0;
+
+    g_return_val_if_fail (MM_IS_PORT_SERIAL_SIT (self), 0);
+
+    g_hash_table_iter_init (&iter, self->priv->pending);
+    while (g_hash_table_iter_next (&iter, NULL, &value)) {
+        Pending *pending = value;
+        gsize    i;
+
+        for (i = 0; i < n_ids; i++) {
+            if (pending->expected_id == ids[i]) {
+                n++;
+                break;
+            }
+        }
+    }
+    return n;
+}
+
 MMSitMessage *
 mm_port_serial_sit_command_finish (MMPortSerialSit  *self,
                                    GAsyncResult     *res,
